{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"20. The Path","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp273-289'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 273–289 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Maggavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>20. The Path </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Path Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp273'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcasatabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Maggānaṭṭhaṅgiko seṭṭho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Of paths, the eightfold is the best; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The best of paths is the Eightfold; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>saccānaṁ caturo padā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>of truths, the four statements; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>of truths, the one in four steps. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Virāgo seṭṭho dhammānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>dispassion is the best of things, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The best of qualities is dispassion; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dvipadānañca cakkhumā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and the Clear-eyed One is the best of humans. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>of bipeds, the one who sees. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp274'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Eseva maggo natthañño, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'><em>This</em> is the path, there is no other </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>This is the path - there is no other - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dassanassa visuddhiyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for the purification of vision. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>for obtaining vision and purity. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etañhi tumhe paṭipajjatha, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You all must practice this, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Therefore, follow this path </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mārassetaṁ pamohanaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>it is the way to baffle Māra. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>which confuses Māra. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp275'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etañhi tumhe paṭipannā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When you all are practicing this, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When you have followed this path </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dukkhassantaṁ karissatha; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll make an end of suffering. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>you will end suffering. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Akkhāto vo mayā maggo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I have explained the path to you </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>I have explained the path for you; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aññāya sallakantanaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for extracting the thorn with wisdom. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by means of knowledge the sting is eased. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp276'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tumhehi kiccamātappaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You yourselves must do the work, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is by you that the effort must be made; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>akkhātāro tathāgatā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the Realized Ones just show the way. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the Truth-Finders just explain. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paṭipannā pamokkhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Meditators practicing absorption </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those who have followed the path become free </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>jhāyino mārabandhanā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are released from Māra’s bonds. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>from the bonds of Māra. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp277'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aniccalakkhaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sabbe saṅkhārā aniccā”ti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>All conditions are impermanent—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Everything is impermanent - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yadā paññāya passati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when this is seen with wisdom, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when one sees this with wisdom, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha nibbindati dukkhe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one grows disillusioned with suffering: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one becomes disenchanted with suffering; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>esa maggo visuddhiyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>this is the path to purity. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this is the path to purity. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp278'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dukkhalakkhaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sabbe saṅkhārā dukkhā”ti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>All conditions are suffering—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Everything is unsatisfying - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yadā paññāya passati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when this is seen with wisdom, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when one sees this with wisdom </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha nibbindati dukkhe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one grows disillusioned with suffering: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one becomes disenchanted with suffering; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>esa maggo visuddhiyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>this is the path to purity. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this is the path to purity. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp279'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Anattalakkhaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sabbe dhammā anattā”ti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>All things are not-self—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Everything is impersonal - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yadā paññāya passati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when this is seen with wisdom, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when one sees this with wisdom, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Atha nibbindati dukkhe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one grows disillusioned with suffering: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one becomes disenchanted with suffering; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>esa maggo visuddhiyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>this is the path to purity. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this is the path to purity. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp280'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Padhānakammikatissattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uṭṭhānakālamhi anuṭṭhahāno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>They don’t get going when it’s time to start; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Not rising to the occasion when it is time to do so, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yuvā balī ālasiyaṁ upeto; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they’re young and strong, but given to sloth. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>young and strong, but indolent, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṁsannasaṅkappamano kusīto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Their mind depressed in sunken thought, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>aimless, and lazy, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paññāya maggaṁ alaso na vindati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>lazy and slothful, they can’t discern the path. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the indolent one does not find the path of wisdom. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp281'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sūkarapetavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vācānurakkhī manasā susaṁvuto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Guarded in speech, restrained in mind, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>With speech controlled and mind well-restrained, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāyena ca nākusalaṁ kayirā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>doing no unskillful bodily deed. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and doing nothing harmful with the body, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ete tayo kammapathe visodhaye, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Purify these three ways of performing deeds, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>purify these three paths of karma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ārādhaye maggamisippaveditaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and win the path known to seers. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and accomplish the path demonstrated by the seer. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp282'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Poṭṭhilattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yogā ve jāyatī bhūri, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>From meditation springs wisdom, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Commitment produces abundance, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ayogā bhūrisaṅkhayo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>without meditation, wisdom ends. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a lack of commitment completely eliminates it. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etaṁ dvedhāpathaṁ ñatvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Knowing these two paths—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Knowing these two paths </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhavāya vibhavāya ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>of progress and decline—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>which lead to existence and non-existence, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tathāttānaṁ niveseyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you should conduct yourself </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one should settle oneself accordingly </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yathā bhūri pavaḍḍhati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so that wisdom grows. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and cultivate abundance. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp283'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcamahallakabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vanaṁ chindatha mā rukkhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cut down the jungle, not just a tree; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Cut down the forest, not the tree; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vanato jāyate bhayaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>from the jungle springs fear. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the forest produces danger. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Chetvā vanañca vanathañca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having cut down jungle and snarl, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When you have cut down the forest and its undergrowth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nibbanā hotha bhikkhavo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>be free of jungles, mendicants! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>you will have no forest, monks. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp284'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yāva hi vanatho na chijjati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>So long as the vine, no matter how small, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>As long as the undergrowth has not been cut down, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Aṇumattopi narassa nārisu; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that ties a man to women is not cut, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>even if only a tiny amount is left, then whether one is a man or a woman </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paṭibaddhamanova tāva so, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>his mind remains trapped, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one will be bound to it, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vaccho khīrapakova mātari. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a calf suckling its mother. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like a calf sucking milk from its mother. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp285'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Suvaṇṇakārattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ucchinda sinehamattano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Cut out affection for oneself, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Cut off self-cherishing, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kumudaṁ sāradikaṁva pāṇinā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like plucking an autumn lotus. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like plucking a lotus in autumn. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Santimaggameva brūhaya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Foster only the path to peace, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Practice the peaceful path to Nibbāna </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nibbānaṁ sugatena desitaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the extinguishment the Holy One taught. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>as taught by the Heavenly One. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp286'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Mahādhanavāṇijavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Idha vassaṁ vasissāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Here I will stay for the rains; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>“Here I will spend the rainy season, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>idha hemantagimhisu; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>here for winter, here the summer”; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>here the winter, here the summer.” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Iti bālo vicinteti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>thus the fool thinks, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>This is how a fool thinks, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>antarāyaṁ na bujjhati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>not realizing the danger. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>not aware of the obstacle. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp287'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kisāgotamīvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Taṁ puttapasusammattaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>As a mighty flood sweeps away a sleeping village, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Intoxicated with children and cattle, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>byāsattamanasaṁ naraṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>death steals away a man </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a person with mind attached; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Suttaṁ gāmaṁ mahoghova, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who dotes on children and cattle, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like a great flood sweeping away a sleeping village, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>maccu ādāya gacchati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>his mind caught up in them. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>such a person is swept away by death. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp288'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Paṭācārāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na santi puttā tāṇāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Children provide you no shelter, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is no safety in children, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na pitā nāpi bandhavā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor does father, nor relatives. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>parents, or kin; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Antakenādhipannassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When you’re seized by the terminator, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when one is seized by the Ender, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi ñātīsu tāṇatā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>there’s no shelter in family. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>there is no safety in relatives. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp289'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etamatthavasaṁ ñatvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Knowing the reason for this, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Having understood this issue, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>paṇḍito sīlasaṁvuto; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>astute, and ethically restrained, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the wise person, moral and self-restrained, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nibbānagamanaṁ maggaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one would quickly clear the path </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>quickly purifies the path </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>khippameva visodhaye. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that leads to extinguishment. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>that leads to Nibbāna. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Maggavaggo vīsatimo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
